根据现象进行分析： V1118 Ori We have observed the EXOr V1118 Ori in the near IR at Campo Imperatore (Italy) telescope, obtaining the following magnitudes:   

MJD 53449.2501, magJ = 11.16;   
MJD 53463.2504, magJ = 10.79;   
MJD 53475.2691, magJ = 10.94;   

MJD 53449.2517, magK = 9.79;   
MJD 53463.2489, magK = 9.48;   
MJD 53475.2708, magK = 9.53.   

The values are calibrated using 2MASS catalog and errors are of the order of 0.01mag in both bands. In the near IR, the object does not appear in its declining phase after the unusual outburst recently observed in the V band (Williams & Heathcote IAUC # 8460 ). The observed colour [J-K] of about 1.35 mag is very similar to that of the FUOri objects (Molinari, Liseau & Lorenzetti, 1993). Other IR observations are encouraged and we will continue such monitoring program. 2005-06-08 08:16:00

根据现象进行分析： GASP detection of a high optical state of the blazar PKS 1510-08 With reference to ATEL #1199 reporting on the possible detection at gamma-ray energies of the blazar PKS 1510-08, the GLAST-AGILE Support Program (GASP) of the Whole Earth Blazar Telescope (WEBT) reports on the recent observation of a very bright optical state of this blazar. The source brightened in the first half of August, reaching a level comparable to the outburst of 1996 (see Raiteri et al. 1998, A&AS, 127, 445), and it appears now in a dimming phase. Some preliminary data are: 
R = 16.37 +/- 0.02 on August 3, 2007 (Crimean Observatory);   
R = 15.04 +/- 0.02 on August 15, 2007 (Crimean Observatory);   
R = 15.52 +/- 0.05 on August 31, 2007 (Armenzano Observatory);   
R = 15.85 +/- 0.05 on September 1, 2007 (Armenzano Observatory);   
R = 15.87 +/- 0.05 on September 2, 2007 (Armenzano Observatory). 2007-09-04 09:24:00

根据现象进行分析： ESO VLT Optical spectroscopy of BL LAc objects: 5 new redshifts  We presents results for Optical spectroscopy of BL Lac candidates performed with the ESO VLT equipped with FORS2. Observations were performed between April and June 2008. We were able to determine new redshift from emission/absorption lines for 5 objects: 
OJ -131: z=0.138, BL Lac, from the detection of MgII, [OII], Hbeta and [OIII] in emission; 
1ES 1106+244: z=0.482, BL Lac, from the detection of CaII H&K and G band in absorption. This is in agreement with the imaging redshift z=0.46+/-0.2 reported by Sbarufatti et al., 2005, ApJ, 635, 173; 
PKS 1815-553: z=1.628, FSRQ, from the detection of CIV, CII] and MgII in emission; 
PKS 2149+17: z=0.870, BL Lac, from the detection of CII], MgII and [OII] in emission; 
RBS 1899: z=0.607, BL Lac, from the detection of CaII H&K in absorption. 2009-07-09 19:58:00

